--- !u!114 &1428787389
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1428787386}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7d20f73aabcb4cfbaac49363662be3e1, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueController
  currentDialogueIndex: 0
  textStartOffset: 0
  dialogues:
  - texts:
    - The engraving on the wall is being imaged by some kind of machine.
    advanceDialogueIndex: 0
    canvasDelayOffset: 0
  - texts:
    - '<<// :: SPEECH SYNTHESIS HASH f92c69d0dcd5287367ced9b5d3d679792b2fdca408292e37c4f6ed76b825578c '
    - Hello. Do not be alarmed. I am Diamber. I am the autonomous administrator of
      this system -- the Glyph.
    - The Glyph and myself were just brought online after an extended outage. I am
      attempting to diagnose the cause.
    - ...
    - The upstream <color=#6EEDFF>Terminals</color> were offline? And you reactivated
      them? Quite a significant development.
    - Those <color=#6EEDFF>Terminals</color> supply the <color=#6EEDFF>leyline signal</color>
      to the entire Mountain. If they failed, the entire network is now down.
    - Please, take this.
    advanceDialogueIndex: 1
    canvasDelayOffset: 0
  - texts:
    - I have given you a Glyphstone, a device of my own design.
    - The Glyph's geometry depicts the <color=#6EEDFF>leylines</color> that run across
      the land.
    - If you spread the <color=#6EEDFF>signal</color> further, the network could
      possibly restabilize. The Glyphstone I provided you will help you follow the
      <color=#6EEDFF>leylines</color>.
    - I would be grateful for your contribution to my directive.
    advanceDialogueIndex: 1
    canvasDelayOffset: 0
  - texts:
    - The Glyph and its expansive Mountain network were built by our forebears.
    - It acted as a relay that synthetically strengthened Amadea's light, staving
      off primordial forces of chaos.
    - The system was designed to be robust, though it seems the turning of the age
      makes folly of such attempts to resist nature.
    - Without her will, the world's unmaking is inevitable.
    advanceDialogueIndex: 1
    canvasDelayOffset: 0
  - texts:
    - If you wish to leave this place, the only way is further up the Mountain.
    - The Glyphstone will guide the way. Good luck.
    advanceDialogueIndex: 0
    canvasDelayOffset: 0
  DialogueName: 
  LookAtOverride: {fileID: 1982441202}
  CameraY: 0.45
  canvasDelay: 0
  cameraFollowOffsetLerp: 0
